  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 222 AM CDT Sat Aug 8 2026\n\nUpper-level ridging will strengthen with a slight build in heights \nover west Texas 7and southeast New Mexico Monday and Tuesday. The \nridge will become more centered over Texas by Wednesday before this \nfeature becomes more oriented from the southern Plains to the Gulf \nCoast states by the latter part of the week. The general take-away \nis that temperatures will stay hot each day through the extended \nforecast period, with daily highs forecast to reach up to 100-105 \ndegrees over much of the forecast area Tuesday-Thursday. A few \nlocations along the Rio Grande may range between 105-110 degrees. \nThese hot temperatures will bring increased heat-related concerns, \nso be sure to take frequent breaks and stay hydrated if spending \ntime outdoors during the hottest part of the day next week. \nIncreased moisture along the western periphery of the ridge will \nbring potential for isolated to scattered showers and thunderstorms \nover the higher terrain areas of the western CWA Wednesday through \nFriday. Isolated to scattered convection may also develop into \nportions of southeast New Mexico and the Permian Basin by Friday \ngiven weak impulses on the western side of the broad ridge axis. \nPOPs generally remain between 20-30% at best late next week, \nexcept slightly higher coverage (30-50%) in the mountains. \nTemperatures may trend slightly lower in the 90s to around 100 \ndegrees for most by Friday.",
